# Google Drive integration (optional).
#
# When both are set, the Studio shows "Open from Drive" / "Save to Drive"
# buttons next to the local Import / Export buttons. When unset, the
# Drive UI hides entirely — the rest of the app works as usual.
#
# Local dev: copy this file to `.env.local` (gitignored) and fill in.
# Production (GitHub Pages): set GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID + GOOGLE_API_KEY as
# repository secrets; the Pages workflow exports them with the VITE_*
# prefix at build time so Vite inlines the values into the bundle.
#
# Setup (one-time, per environment):
#   1. Go to https://console.cloud.google.com/ and create a project.
#   2. APIs & Services → Library → enable "Google Drive API" and
#      "Google Picker API".
#   3. APIs & Services → Credentials:
#        - Create OAuth 2.0 Client ID (type: Web application).
#          Authorized JavaScript origins: your deploy origin(s)
#          (e.g. https://kukuistudio.com, http://localhost:5174).
#        - Create API Key. Restrict to Google Picker API for safety.
#   4. APIs & Services → OAuth consent screen: fill in app name,
#      support email, logo, privacy URL (/privacy), Terms (optional).
#      Scope: drive.file (this is the minimum-privilege scope; we
#      only touch files we created or files the user explicitly
#      picks via Google Picker).
#   5. Copy the Client ID and API Key below.

VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
VITE_GOOGLE_API_KEY=
# Google Cloud project NUMBER (12-digit, NOT the project ID slug).
# Required by the Picker when using `drive.file` scope — without it
# the dialog opens empty because Drive can't filter to "files this app
# created". Find it on the Cloud Console dashboard under "Project
# info → Project number".
VITE_GOOGLE_APP_ID=
